--TEST--
`echo`, `.`, an interpolated piece and `.=` agree that `bytes`, `array<T>`, an enum case and a `void` call have no string form — `rule:types/conversion`, `rule:types/conversion`, `rule:enums/no-class-machinery`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:types/conversion`'s "anything → `string`" row is total for scalars and needs
// `Stringable` for an object. These four types it does not reach at all, and
// the four *implicit* sites — `echo`, `.`, an interpolated piece and `.=` —
// agree on refusing them, being one check.
enum Mode: int {
    Read = 1,
}

class Helper {
    public static function nothing(): void {}
}

bytes $by = "ab" as bytes;
array<int> $xs = [1, 2];
Mode $m = Mode::Read;

// One type per site, so the agreement asserted is across the sites as well
// as across the types.
echo $by;
string $s1 = "" . $xs;
string $s2 = "x{$m}y";
string $s3 = "";
$s3 .= Helper::nothing();

// The explicit conversion is the answer in each case, and stays legal: ADR
// 0009 § 3 grants `bytes as string` and `rule:enums/no-class-machinery` grants `$case as int`.
echo $by as string, $m as int, "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0707]: `bytes` has no string form
   --> %s:20:6
   |
20 | echo $by;
   |      ^^^ converted to `string` here
   = help: `rule:types/conversion` makes that conversion explicit, because which encoding the octets are in is a decision — `$b as string`

error[E0707]: `array<int>` has no string form
   --> %s:21:19
   |
21 | string $s1 = "" . $xs;
   |                   ^^^ converted to `string` here
   = help: an `array<T>` has no text of its own; render it — `Core\Json::encode($a)` — or build the string from its elements

error[E0707]: `Mode` has no string form
   --> %s:22:17
   |
22 | string $s2 = "x{$m}y";
   |                 ^^ converted to `string` here
   = help: an enum case is a named integer (`rule:enums/no-class-machinery`), not text — `$case as int`, or a member of your own that names it

error[E0707]: `void` has no string form
   --> %s:24:8
   |
24 | $s3 .= Helper::nothing();
   |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ converted to `string` here
   = help: a call that returns `void` has no value at all, so there is nothing here to print

error: aborting due to 4 errors
